	"notes": "The hub's music (the owner, 2026-11-18: a somewhat sad piece of background music playing in the hub), one layer: E minor at 66 beats a minute, 32 bars (116 s) round, in four eights. Em C Am B, the bells alone, a falling tune that ends each line on a held note; then G D Em C and Am Em C B, the low strings taking the tune under a bell or two; the first tune again with the strings holding under it; and a last walk down, Em over E and D, C, B, then Am Em B and a bar of Em standing still before it comes round. The bells are far back (the owner, 2026-11-18, after hearing them up front: way more subtle), 13 dB under where they were, so the pad and the strings carry the piece. A wide room, nothing above 6 kHz, and 2 dB under the music's level (gain -2): the hub is where a player rests and reads, over the island's wind."
